 while slowly whistling amournful tune. This can be done normally or in duress: as a backup, a piercingwhistle or shouted chant suffices to trigger the domain even under attack.● Non-Enclosed Space: Upon activation, the domain spreads immediately throughthe real environment[1]. Ethereal water rises (coating floors and objects) and thesky darkens to reveal the chosen moon phase. No barrier walls appear; insteadthe entire area is haunted by the domain’s water and sky. This mimics Sukuna’sinnate domain which is “painted on air”[1], allowing enemies to move freely whilestill affected.● Phases of the Moon: I choose one of 8 moon phases (listed below) during theincantation. The sky shifts accordingly (e.g. a fiery red for Blood Moon) andsustains that phase. Changing the phase mid-battle requires a quick additionalchant and extra energy, risking concentration. Each phase modifies the domain’seffects significantly (detailed later).● Guaranteed Hits: All offensive actions tied to the domain (sonic blasts, spiritstrikes, etc.) automatically hit targets within range, reflecting the guaranteed-hitrule of lethal domains[4]. For example, if I send forth a Sound Slash or throw thethistle spear with a battle cry, it cannot miss. This is a fundamental aspect, akin toSukuna’s assured slashes[4].● Area and Scale (Tiered): The domain’s effective radius is tiered by energy. Tier 1(~20–50m) floods a single building; Tier 2 (~100–150m) spans multiple blocks;Tier 3 (~200m+) can cover a large urban area (on par with Sukuna’s domain[1]).Enemies farther out feel the pull of the cursed moonlight (slowed movement,chilling sensation) but are safe from direct effects.● Water of Death: The domain’s water continuously saps cursed energy and vitalityfrom foes wading in it. It acts like an aura: each round spent immersed weakensenemies by a small percent of their energy. This compounding drain fits thenecromantic theme and helps ensure the final “soul-tug” kill.Black Thistle Polearm● Design & Lore: The caster wields a dark thistle polearm (inspired by Garth Nix’sfree-magic flora). It’s a long, blackwood shaft wrapped in thorny iron, with adual-ended spearhead. Like Abhorsen’s bells forged in Death’s waters[5], thispolearm is forged in necromantic rites – its wood was quenched in the “Waters ofDeath,” binding it to the domain’s magic. It’s said that the thistle metal is infusedwith free-magic poison, making it lethal to spirits and mortal alike.● Melee Use: In melee, the polearm deals heavy slash/pierce damage. It canimpale cursed spirits or fend off enemies trying to close in. Every strike is imbuedwith the domain’s power: even a glancing blow summons tiny spectral thorns thatlatch onto the victim, continuing to drain health (similar to Sukuna’s slashescausing aftereffects[6]).● Sound Conduction: The polearm doubles as an amplifier. It has hollows or runesalong the shaft that resonate with the caster’s voice. By chanting into the pole, Ican launch focused sound lances: e.g. speaking “Spatium!” through it sends atapered sonic spear that tears through the air. The weapon essentially works likea blowgun or resonator.● Ranged Capability: The caster can also throw the polearm. When thrown with achant, it returns (like a boomerang), trailing a spiral of cursed energy. It creates adevastating Shockwave Explosion on impact (as if the pole violently resonatesupon hitting ground). This gives a powerful ranged option, yet the pole alwaysreturns to her hand magically.● Special Atack – Thistle Bloom: She can strike the ground with the pole, causingghostly thistle vines to erupt in an area. These vines entangle and spike foes (acrowd-control zone). This is a signature move requiring a loud shout (“Spinaregnant! – “Thorns reign!”) and a vigorous slam.Sound-Based Attack MechanicsAll attacks in Lunar Funeral Hymn use sound as their medium. Cursed speech (voice),whistles, and bells function like spells, each with JJK analogues:● Cursed Commands: Short shouts or words carry cursed force. For instance:● “Stay!” freezes a target’s feet in swirling water (akin to a binding domain rule).● “Shater!” emits a concussive blast that can destroy obstacles (similar in effect toSukuna’s Divine Flame that pulverizes surroundings[7], but here acoustically).● Whistles & Chants: Melodic tones produce elemental effects:● A high-pitched whistle creates a Frostblade (freezing sonic arc) under SnowMoon.● A low chant booms out a Soundquake (rock-throwing quake wave).These are analogous to known techniques (e.g. Jogo’s powerful sound). Each isscalable by tier (Tier 1: small jolt; Tier 3: city-shaking boom).● Bell-Tones: Three ceremonial bells convey classic Abhorsen functions[8][9]:● Binder Bell (deep tone) forces obedience or paralysis (like “No Escape”boundary).● Sleeper Bell (gentle tone) casts sleep.● Grave Bell (bassy funeral toll) drains life from enemies in range.Striking combinations yields compound effects.● Atack Types:● Sound Slash: Swinging the polearm with a yell (“Cut!”) sends a blade ofcompressed sound. This acts like a ranged slash attack with enhancedcut-through (cannot miss, guaranteed to draw blood).● Echo Sphere: Whistling forms a shimmering sphere of sonic energy around apoint. After a brief flash, it implodes like a grenade, damaging all within(area-stun).● Roaring Wave: A roar amplifies through the domain’s water to create a wall ofshock-energy that sweeps forward, toppling anyone hit (similar to a large-scalewind blast).● Mermaid Diagram – Sound to Efect:flowchart LRSpeak(Voice Command) -->|“Stay!”| Freeze[Bind Water]Speak -->|“Shatter!”| Smash[Concussive Blast]Whistle(High Tone) -->|“Frost!”| Slash[Sonic Ice Blade]Hum(Low Chant) -->|“Quake!”| Shock[Ground Shockwave]BellBinder -->|“Obey!”| Bind[Dominate Paralyze]BellSleeper -->|“Sleep!”| Sleep[Induce Sleep]BellGrave -->|“Wither!”| Drain[Life Drain Aura]This mapping shows each sound input yielding a specific domain attack or effect, allguaranteed-hit style.Moon Phase EffectsEach phase dramatically alters the domain’s power. Effects are tier-scaled (Tier 1 mild,Tier 3 extreme) and designed to synergize with sound/spirit attacks:1. 2. Blood Moon (Crimson Red): The water turns thick red. All strikes causehemorrhagic wounds: targets bleed profusely after each hit (stacking damageover time). Chants like “Sanguis!” (Latin for blood) draw forth red waves that slicelike blades. Tier 3: A wave of blood can engulf multiple enemies, nearlyincapacitating them. Example: Under Blood Moon, spearing an enemy mightleave them spurting blood, making their next move weaker.Blue Moon (Twin Blue Orbs): Two moons fill the sky. Power doubles: each bellstrike or chant effect is effectively repeated. For example, echoing a commandcreates two simultaneous shockwaves. Tier 3: Certain attacks echo infinitely for asecond (e.g. a continual barrage of thistle-projections). Example: Hitting a belltwice in quick succession causes two Sleep-wave circles.3. 4. 5. Wolf Moon (Wolf Silhouetes): Ghostly wolves prowl. The domain summons wolfspirits that aid in combat (harassing enemies and defending allies). The castergains enhanced tracking: sound attacks home in on marked foes. Howlcommands (“Ulvus!”) give minor speed buffs. Tier 3: A pack of spectral wolvescan pounce on an enemy, dealing heavy cumulative damage. Example: UnderWolf Moon, whistling a shrill cry might cause a wolf spirit to sprint at a foe,immobilizing them.Snow Moon (Pale Blue): A frosty aura covers all. Water and sounds gain iceatributes: Sound Slash becomes a freezing blade (slowing hit foes); EchoSphere bursts into ice shards. Tier 3: The entire floor can become ice (enemiesmust succeed on checks to stay upright). Example: A low chant might create awall of ice spikes with each pulse.Harvest Moon (Golden Harvest): A warm orange glow. The domain leachesenergy from enemies to strengthen itself. Each attack partially heals the caster orsustains summoned spirits (like drawing life from foes). Tier 3: The caster cancast “Reap