Phase --> ColdPhase --> Crow_Slow[Cold Moon: Slow/Aura]_Fear[Crow Moon: Summon Crows/Panic]Spirits & Soul-Tugging● Wraiths and Revenants: The domain’s water teems with dormant spirit-forms.With certain sounds, I can call them forth: for example, a harsh whistle mightanimate a water-wraith that grips a foe from below. These spirits latch ontoenemies’ souls. Each successful latch drains an extra chunk of vitality (like anongoing life-drain).● Gossamer Shade: A fleeting, nearly invisible spirit that flits behind a target,dimming their senses. It halves the target’s reaction speed each round untildispelled.● Thorn Wraith: A bulky specter of tangled thorns (ties in with the polearm theme)that ensnares anyone in melee range, enabling a guaranteed follow-up strike bythe caster.● Soul Extraction: Once a foe is sufficiently weakened (near 0 HP or cursed energydrained), I can order a spirit: e.g. “Absorbe!”. A spirit will attempt to tug the soulout. This is a domain-executive move – if successful, the enemy is slain outright.Against Sukuna-tier foes, it might require 2-3 consecutive tugs (Sukuna’s heavycursed energy gives partial resistance). The tug is faster and stronger under Coldand Crow Moons (as fits their themes). Failing a tug attempt forces me to waitone turn before trying again, preventing instant kills.Interaction with Malevolent Shrine● Domain Clash: In a clash, Lunar Funeral Hymn is designed to win ~65% of thetime. This is achieved by both mechanical edge and narrative factors:● Wide Area Advantage: At equal tier, Lunar Hymn can extend slightly beyondSukuna’s shrine radius. E.g. if both are Tier 3, Lunar Hymn might cover 220m vsSukuna’s 200m[1], letting it strike Sukuna’s domain from outside.● Sound vs Slash: Since Sukuna’s shrine relies on slashes, Lunar’s water canpartially dampen those slashes. We assume that in 65% of equal-energyclashes, Sukuna’s slashes are slightly deflected by the cursed water (forcing himto use more energy per slash). Conversely, Lunar’s