Sukuna lunged, his Malevolent Shrine slashing, but the Crow Moon gave her the edge: the crows swarmed, the water slowed his movements, and a ghostly tendril nearly ripped at his heart.

Yet it wasn’t victory he wanted. It was her. Her defiance, her power, the way she met him eye to eye without flinching.

