He grinned, teeth flashing. “Such power… and yet, so defiant. I will have you.”

“And try if you dare,” she countered, black thistle resting against her shoulder, spectral water curling around her like a cloak.

The moonlight of the shrine mingled with Sukuna’s aura, a violent yet beautiful dance of energy and shadow. Two forces, equally lethal, now bound by curiosity, desire, and a dangerous respect.

The chapter closed on tension, a mutual recognition: they had found their match—one in power, one in spirit, one in danger, and one in… affection, strange as it was.

Little Ghost. Menka. Names that would echo in their battles to come.

