His eyes gleamed.

“No,” he said.
“Not yet.”

The Return
The moment shattered.

A presence surged at the edge of the estate—sharp, familiar.

Leora felt it instantly.

So did Sukuna.

His expression didn’t change.

But something beneath it did.

“…Persistent,” he murmured.

Leora was already moving.

Ignoring the weakness.

Ignoring the pain.

She stepped out into the open courtyard—

Wind caught her hair, the sky stretching pale above—

And they were there.

Amon.

Wilhelm.

Again.

The Plea
Amon stepped forward immediately.

No hesitation this time.

No careful distance.

“Leora,” he said, voice rough, urgent. “Please.”

That word—

It landed differently than anything else he’d said before.

She stilled.

“…You shouldn’t have come back.”

