Chapter XLIX — What Is His Is Not Touched
The first incident is small.

So small it almost doesn’t matter.

Leora is standing in the outer courtyard when it happens.

She shouldn’t be there.

Not by his standards.

But she is.

The air is warm, the late afternoon sun spilling across the stone, catching in the edges of her hair, softening the sharpness she usually carries.

For once—

she looks almost human.

There are servants nearby.

At a distance.

Careful.

Always careful.

They do not speak unless spoken to.

Do not approach unless summoned.

But one of them—

new—

does not understand that yet.

