Low.

At her waist.

Firm.

Anchoring.

Leora stills.

Because this—

this is not restraint.

This is possession.

“You don’t leave the estate,” he repeats.

Her breath catches slightly.

“…And if I do?”

Sukuna’s gaze lowers—

just briefly—

to where his hand rests against her.

Then returns to her eyes.

“Then I remove whatever made you think you could.”

Silence.

Heavy.

Leora studies him.

This isn’t play.

This isn’t tension.

This is—

real.

“…You’re overcorrecting,” she says.

“No.”

“You are.”

Her hand lifts—

resting lightly against his chest now.

Grounding him.

Or trying to.

“This isn’t just about me,” she continues. “Something scared you.”

That—

almost earns a reaction.

Almost.

But Sukuna doesn’t deny it.

Doesn’t confirm it either.

Instead—

his grip tightens slightly.

“You don’t understand the scale of what’s trying to take you.”

Her eyes narrow.

“…Then explain it.”

“I will.”

A pause.

“When it’s irrelevant.”

She exhales sharply.

“That’s not how this works.”

“It is now.”

Again.

Final.

And this time—

he doesn’t leave room for argument.

The second incident is not small.

