The man smiles faintly.

Unbothered.

“I’ve been waiting for you.”

Not Sukuna.

Her.

Leora feels it.

That pull—

stronger now.

Different from Sukuna.

Not forceful.

Inviting.

“…You shouldn’t resist it,” the man continues softly. “You’ll only make it harder on yourself.”

Sukuna moves.

Fast.

Violently.

One step—

and he’s in front of him.

The ground cracks under the force.

“You’re done speaking.”

The man doesn’t move.

Doesn’t defend.

Just watches.

“…You haven’t secured her yet,” he says calmly.

That—

that lands.

Sukuna’s cursed energy spikes—

sharp—

lethal—

“Say that again.”

