Relentless.

Each strike heavier than the last.

Each movement faster.

Sharper.

But the man—

keeps smiling.

“You’re strong,” he says. “As expected.”

Sukuna’s grin is feral now.

“You’re nothing.”

Another strike—

this one lands.

Fully.

The man’s body distorts—

breaks—

then reforms.

“…But not enough.”

Silence.

Then—

Sukuna laughs.

Low.

Violent.

“Good.”

Because now—

he’s interested.

Behind him—

Leora watches.

And for the first time—

she understands.

This is what he meant.

This is what’s coming.

The man steps back finally.

Not retreating.

Choosing distance.

“…I’ll return,” he says simply.

His gaze flicks to Leora one last time.

“And next time—”

A pause.

“—you’ll come willingly.”

